{
    "background_story": "Jude was a brilliant and reclusive astronomer who spent most of his life studying the mysteries of the universe. His obsession with understanding the intricacies of celestial mechanics led him to make a groundbreaking discovery. While pouring over ancient texts and star charts, Jude stumbled upon an obscure reference to the steradian, a unit of measurement for solid angles. Intrigued, he devoted himself to unlocking its secrets. His tireless work paid off when he successfully applied the concept of steradians to predict a rare astronomical event - a planetary alignment that would reveal a hidden pattern in the cosmos. Jude's findings sent shockwaves through the scientific community, earning him international recognition and cementing his place among the greatest minds in astronomy.",
